\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Horrific nature of the leech farm}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram is losing his shit shit.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora picked up Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s paintbrush and rolled it\u8217\'92s handle between her fingers. Her sly, expectant look pricked Mandri\u8217\'92s skin}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 I want to leave this hole, but I don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know anyone around here. Do you have a place I could stay?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Uh, no, not really. I mean, I don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t think you\u8217\'92d find it comfortable.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Dying shrieks. Vigram chewing it out.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Inquiring eyes.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I have a farm,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s not much of a farm. There\u8217\'92s no house or anything. I don\u8217\'92t think a girl like yourself would find it comfortable. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You don\u8217\'92t know anything about me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Not true. Look at her. That if she thought she could be comfortable under, she didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know anything about herself.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Alright. You\u8217\'92re welcome to whatever shade you can find on my farm. But I can\u8217\'92t leave yet. Vigram hasn\u8217\'92t paid me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He scraped a slap of yellow ochre back into its little clay jar. There was enough untouched pigment left on the palette for at least four more of these awkward lessons.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora pulls out money.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is this enough?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
